    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **69 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**, BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 including the new `Cp57Tests`.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe `POST /api/owners` create pipeline already emitted audit lines (`AUDIT` logger) via `AuditOwnerCreated` and `EmitOwnerCreatedEvent`. The spec asked for a welcome notification on the separate `NOTIFY` logger carrying the owner id and memberId.\n\n**1. New function class** \u2014 `EnqueueWelcomeNotification.java` (one public method, reads the saved owner via `@Val Owner`):\n```java\nprivate static final Logger NOTIFY = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"NOTIFY\");\npublic void service(@Val Owner owner) {\n    NOTIFY.info(\"welcome owner id={} memberId={}\", owner.getId(), owner.getMemberId());\n}\n```\n\n**2. Wired it into `owners.POST.yml`** as a `notifyWelcome` step inserted after `emitEvent` and before `respond`, under the same `govern: [ transaction ]`. Placing it after `save` guarantees the owner has a generated id and its memberId assigned.\n\nThe test confirms the line: `NOTIFY - welcome owner id=11 memberId=NSW2616E6609E3`.",
